   "text": {
    "L1": "A number line shows fractions as jumps from zero.",
    "L2": "Split each whole into equal spaces. Three jumps of one quarter reach 3/4.",
    "L3": "Count the spaces between marks, not the marks themselves.",
    "L4": "Fractions can be more than one. Five quarters means five jumps, so 5/4 is past 1.",
    "L5": "To make a mixed fraction, divide the numerator by the denominator.",
    "L6": "For 11/4, the quotient is 2 and the remainder is 3, so the answer is 2 3/4.",
    "L7": "To change back, multiply wholes by the denominator, add the parts, and keep the denominator.",
    "L8": "Now place 17/5: go to 3, then make 2 fifth-jumps toward 4."
   },
